"""
chemistry_companion/chemistry_companion.py
==========================================
CLI entry point — Phase 1 + Phase 2 spectral commands.

Subcommands
-----------
  analyse     Single-molecule full analysis pipeline
  batch       Batch analysis from CSV/SMILES list
  ir          IR absorption band prediction
  hnmr        Estimated 1H NMR shifts
  cnmr        Estimated 13C NMR shifts
  funcgroups  Functional group detection
  image       2D structure image export
  export      Export descriptors to CSV / JSON / XLSX
  demo        Run built-in demo (Benzene / Aspirin / Caffeine / Ibuprofen)
  version     Print version and dependency info

Usage examples
--------------
  python chemistry_companion.py analyse --smiles "c1ccccc1" --name Benzene
  python chemistry_companion.py analyse --iupac caffeine --save-image --export csv
  python chemistry_companion.py batch --file compounds.csv --export csv xlsx
  python chemistry_companion.py ir --smiles "CC(=O)Oc1ccccc1C(=O)O"
  python chemistry_companion.py hnmr --smiles "Cc1ccccc1"
  python chemistry_companion.py cnmr --smiles "Cc1ccccc1"
  python chemistry_companion.py funcgroups --smiles "CC(=O)Oc1ccccc1C(=O)O"
  python chemistry_companion.py image --smiles "c1ccccc1" --output-dir output/
  python chemistry_companion.py export --smiles "c1ccccc1" --formats csv json
  python chemistry_companion.py demo
  python chemistry_companion.py --verbose analyse --smiles "c1ccccc1"

Architecture
------------
Three-layer design, each independently testable:

  run_*()        Pure pipeline functions — no argparse, no sys.exit, importable in tests
  _cmd_*()       Thin CLI shims — unpack args, call run_*(), handle sys.exit codes
  build_parser() Registers all subcommands with full help text

Logging
-------
Centralized via core.logging_utils.configure_logging() wired through
core.config.ChemistryCompanionSettings. Falls back to logging.basicConfig
if the config subsystem is unavailable.

Settings
--------
Reads core.config.get_settings() on startup. Honours environment variables:
  CHEM_COMPANION_LOGGING__LEVEL=DEBUG
  CHEM_COMPANION_DIRECTORIES__OUTPUT_DIR=/tmp/results
  CHEM_COMPANION_IMAGE__WIDTH=800

Scientific notes
----------------
  - NMR shifts are HEURISTIC / APPROXIMATE — not DFT-derived
  - IR bands are FUNCTIONAL-GROUP HEURISTICS — not quantum calculations
  - Docking scores are not experimentally validated
"""

from __future__ import annotations

